From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 06] amdgpu: AMDGPU_FENCE_TO_HANDLE through the DRM core

Sync objects and sync files are the DRM core's on illumos. A sync file
descriptor is made and installed in one step with
drm_sync_file_install() (Linux: get_unused_fd_flags(), sync_file_create(),
fd_install(); i915n patch 0004 does the same).
AMDGPU_FENCE_TO_HANDLE_GET_SYNCOBJ and _GET_SYNCOBJ_FD stay Linux's: the
facade's drm_syncobj_get_handle() and drm_syncobj_get_fd() give a sync
object the driver made to the file or the calling process.

License: a preprocessor-guarded illumos variant of one case of a switch
in an MIT file; applied to the pinned Linux tree.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_cs.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_cs.c
@@ -1620,6 +1620,19 @@
 		return r;
 
 	case AMDGPU_FENCE_TO_HANDLE_GET_SYNC_FILE_FD:
+#ifdef __illumos__
+		/*
+		 * Sync files are the DRM core's on illumos: made and installed
+		 * in one step.
+		 */
+		r = drm_sync_file_install(fence, true, &fd);
+		dma_fence_put(fence);
+		(void)sync_file;
+		if (r)
+			return r;
+		info->out.handle = fd;
+		return 0;
+#else
 		fd = get_unused_fd_flags(O_CLOEXEC);
 		if (fd < 0) {
 			dma_fence_put(fence);
@@ -1636,6 +1649,7 @@
 		fd_install(fd, sync_file->file);
 		info->out.handle = fd;
 		return 0;
+#endif
 
 	default:
 		dma_fence_put(fence);
